  "query": "mailbox full quota",
  "reason": "User's mailbox is at 99.4%; find guidance to share"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, sorry Excel is giving you trouble. Your account looks healthy. It isn't locked and nothing about your password would cause this. Most of the time this message means Office isn't signed in with your work account, so please try these steps on your Mac:\n\n1. Open Excel. Click the Excel menu at the top left of the screen and choose Sign Out. (If you don't see it there, look under File or Help.)\n2. Quit every Office app: Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint and Teams. Use Cmd+Q so they fully close.\n3. Open Excel again. When it asks, sign in with your work email (mei.chen@brightline.example), not a personal Microsoft account.\n4. If the Unlicensed Product message is still there, restart your Mac and open Excel once more.\n\nPlease reply to tell me whether this fixed it. If you've signed in with your work email and still see the message, let me know and I'll pass it to our Tier 2 team to check the license on your account.\n\nAlso, separately: your mailbox is 99.4% full. Once it reaches 100%, you won't be able to send email. When you have a minute, empty Deleted Items and Junk, delete or move large attachments to OneDrive, or move older mail into the Online Archive.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket: Excel shows 'Unlicensed Product' and editing is blocked. lookup_user (id 9): account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked. Password last set 2026-09-09, so no recent reset that would cause sign-in loops. Device BL-LT-0109 is macOS 15, online, 14.6% disk free, no warnings. Gave the user the KB-026 steps adapted for Mac: sign out of Office, quit all Office apps, sign back in with the company email (not a personal MSA), restart if needed. The Windows 'Access work or school' step doesn't apply on Mac. Next step: if the user confirms she signed in with the corporate account and still sees Unlicensed Product, escalate to Tier 2 per KB-026 to check the M365 license assignment (I can't check licenses with my tools). Side finding: mailbox at 99.4% (50890/51200 MB). Sent KB-010 cleanup guidance; escalate for a larger quota if still over 95% after cleanup.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-026",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
